 is a `budget_capped` event. The repository may be public, so the spend it shows is public too; the table holds no agent text or host paths. Scanner failure streaks (#221, the early slice of the digest, #58): each scanner posts one comment on the status issue when a failure streak starts and one when it recovers. A streak starts at the first run that is a guard trip or guard error (reason: the guard rule name or `scan-error`), any other `scan_failed` run (a `timeout` counts as `scan_failed`) or a skip at `max_open`, and ends at the next `ok` run. The posted class is kept in the scanner's `meta` table (key `failure_streak`), so a restart does not repost, and it is written only after the post succeeds. Runs dropped at the global cap and `error` runs neither start nor end a streak. A comment carries the scanner name and the reason class only, never finding text, titles, fingerprints or log lines. The post goes through the effect layer, so a dry-run logs it (`scanner.streak_notice`) and stores no streak. While the status issue number is unknown nothing is posted and the streak is not recorded, so it posts once the issue exists.\ninternal/cli/app.go:18:type Globals struct {\ninternal/cli/app.go-19-\tRepo       string // \"owner/repo\"; validated when set\ninternal/cli/app.go-20-\tConfigPath string // default .ard/config.yaml in the target repo (#11)\ninternal/cli/app.go-21-\tDryRun     bool\ninternal/cli/app.go-22-\tLogLevel   string // debug|info|warn|error, default info\ninternal/cli/app.go-23-}\ninternal/cli/app.go-24-\ninternal/cli/app.go-25-// Env is passed to every command handler.\ninternal/cli/app.go-26-type Env struct {\ninternal/cli/app.go-27-\tGlobals\ninternal/cli/app.go-28-\tLog            *slog.Logger\ninternal/cli/app.go-29-\tStdout, Stderr io.Writer\ninternal/cli/app.go-30-}\ninternal/limits/readings.go:23:type Reading struct {\ninternal/limits/readings.go-24-\tWindow      string    `json:\"window\"`\ninternal/limits/readings.go-25-\tUtilization float64  